<!-- The SHARED BOARD: persistent, multi-user, networked state through the GUI.
     Every element here is the reuse of an existing sophisticated piece:
       · storage is src/dbservice.rs — the WAL-backed persistent database
         (posts survive restarts; MVCC history; the generation-cached reads)
       · post keys are Lamport pairs (lib/lamport.lat's total order), so
         boards on DIFFERENT NODES merge as a G-Set (lib/crdt.lat's playbook):
         sync in any order, converge to the union
       · the widgets are the same Live machinery every tools page uses; the
         new Live.form variant runs its expression only on the button
       · the page memo is keyed by the DATA generation, so one user's post is
         in every other user's very next render — never stale, never slow -->
<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>The Board — shared, persistent, networked</title>
<style>
  :root { --paper:#fbf8f3; --rule:#8e8a7a; --title:#cfcaba; --ink:#1a1320; --accent:#5a1530; --heart:#8a1538; }
  body { font-family:'Ligos', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; max-width:48rem; margin:3rem auto; padding:0 1rem; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ink); background:var(--paper); }
  h1 { font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.03em; color:var(--accent); font-size:2.4rem; margin-bottom:0; }
  .panel { background:var(--paper); border:1.5px solid var(--rule); border-radius:4px; margin:1.4rem 0; box-shadow:0 1px 4px #0001; }
  .panel > .t { background:var(--title); border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--rule); padding:5px 11px; font-weight:700; font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.04em; color:var(--accent); border-radius:4px 4px 0 0; }
  .panel > .b { padding:11px 13px; }
  .lede { margin:.1rem 0 .8rem; color:#473b4a; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:.4rem 0; }
  td, th { border-bottom:1px solid #e4dccc; padding:.32rem .6rem; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; }
  th { color:var(--accent); font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.03em; }
  code { background:#efe9dd; padding:0 .3rem; border-radius:3px; font-family:'DejaVu Sans Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size:.92em; }
  .live { display:inline-flex; gap:.4rem; align-items:baseline; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .live input.li, .live select.li { font-family:inherit; font-size:.95rem; padding:.2rem .45rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:3px; background:#fff; color:var(--ink); }
  .live input[type=range].li { padding:0; vertical-align:middle; accent-color:var(--accent); }
  .live .liv { font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--accent); min-width:2.4em; display:inline-block; font-size:.9rem; }
</style>
<h1>The Board</h1>

<p class="lede">A message board shared by <b>everyone who can reach this node</b> — every
browser tab, every user on the network, the CLI (<code>latte db board …</code>), and
<b>other Orpheus systems</b> via sync. Posts are persistent: they live in the write-ahead
log and survive restarts.</p>

<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Post a message</div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Your post is stamped with a Lamport pair — the time, then this node's
    id as the tie-break — so posts from different machines interleave in one agreed
    order when boards merge.</p>
    {{ Live.form("Db.post(\"board\", author, text)", [["author", "anon"], ["text", "hello, network"]]) }}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">The board</div>
  <div class="b">
    {{ Live.view("Db.board(\"board\", n)", [["n", "20", "~", "5", "50", "5"]]) }}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Connect another system</div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Point this at a peer's address and the two boards reconcile: entries the
    peer has are pulled, entries it lacks are pushed — the G-Set union, idempotent and
    order-independent. Run it from either side, or both; the boards converge. (The same
    operation from a shell: <code>latte db sync http://host:8088 board</code>.)</p>
    {{ Live.form("Db.sync(\"board\", url)", [["url", "http://127.0.0.1:8089"]]) }}
  </div>
</div>

<p>Under the hood: <a href="/docs#the-system">the persistent database</a> ·
<a href="/docs#interaction-nets">the engines</a> · the CRDT and Lamport chapters of the
data-intensive library (<code>lib/crdt.lat</code>, <code>lib/lamport.lat</code>) are the
semantics this page runs on.</p>
